{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc 'cat /tmp/research_notes.md 2>/dev/null | head -200'", "aggregated_output": "# Research Notes: Hierarchical Transport Valuation Speedup\n\n## Goal\nReduce per-case median method time while maintaining NRMSE ≤ 0.01, Spearman ≥ 0.999, top-quarter overlap ≥ 0.98.\n\n## Baseline (canonical)\n- B = 0.5215s aggregate (from protocol.json)\n- My local single-case measurement: ~5.7s for N=3000, M=2000\n  - 3 candidate batches (1024, 1024, 952) × 2 reference batches (1024, 976) = 6 batch pairs\n  - Label cost: ~0.8-1.0s (190 pairs of ~100 samples each)\n  - Per pair: POT sinkhorn ~0.5-0.7s + GeomLoss potentials ~0.13s\n  - 6 × (0.6 + 0.13) ≈ 4.4s + label cost ≈ 5.4s total ≈ matches measurement\n\n## Key Optimization Hypotheses\n\n### H1: Unify dual Sinkhorn solves\nCanonical solves Sinkhorn twice per batch pair:\n- POT `sinkhorn()` for batch-level cost (for inter-batch transport Q)\n- GeomLoss `SamplesLoss(potentials=True)` for point-level potentials\nBoth solve the same Sinkhorn problem. Compute once, extract both coupling and potentials.\nExpected speedup: ~40-50% per batch pair.\n\n### H2: Accelerate label cost computation\n190 GeomLoss calls at ~5ms each = ~1s. Can we:\n- Use POT or simpler distance metric?\n- Use smaller subsets per class?\n- Use a proxy like average class centroid distance?\n\n### H3: Larger batches / fewer pairs\nCurrently 1024 batch size → 6 pairs. \nLarger batches → fewer pairs but each pair more expensive.\nNet effect depends on scalability.\n\n### H4: Log-domain Sinkhorn\nAlready confirmed slightly faster. Use as baseline improvement.\n\n### H5: Approximate the second-level transport\nInter-batch transport Q is small (3x2 matrix). Could we avoid OT here entirely?\nJust use uniform weighting?\n\n## Quality Gates\n- NRMSE ≤ 0.01 (1% error)\n- Spearman ≥ 0.999\n- Top-quarter overlap ≥ 0.98\nThese are fairly loose, so significant approximation should be possible.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/solution/method.py | head -100'", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"v10: Single GeomLoss solve per pair (potentials + batchcost from P reconstruction).\n- Eliminates redundant POT solve\n- Keeps label cost as canonical GeomLoss\n- Computes batchcost from GeomLoss potentials (P = diag(a) K diag(b) form)\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\nfrom geomloss import SamplesLoss\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\nimport ot\n\n\ndef _label_cost(x, y, r, ry):\n    xx = torch.tensor(np.concatenate([x, r]), dtype=torch.float32)\n    yy = np.concatenate([y, ry + 10])\n    W = np.zeros((20, 20), dtype=np.float32)\n    loss = SamplesLoss('sinkhorn', p=2, blur=np.sqrt(.1), debias=False, backend='tensorized')\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n        for i in range(20):\n            for j in range(i + 1, 20):\n                if not (yy == i).any() or not (yy == j).any():\n                    raise ValueError('Initial batch lacks a label support')\n                W[i, j] = W[j, i] = float(loss(xx[yy == i], xx[yy == j]))\n    return W\n\n\ndef value(x, y, r, ry, seed=17, batch_size=1024):\n    torch.set_num_threads(2)\n    x = np.asarray(x, np.float32); r = np.asarray(r, np.float32)\n    y = np.asarray(y, np.int64); ry = np.asarray(ry, np.int64)\n    tx = [np.arange(i, min(i + batch_size, len(x))) for i in range(0, len(x), batch_size)]\n    tr = [np.arange(i, min(i + batch_size, len(r))) for i in range(0, len(r), batch_size)]\n\n    W = _label_cost(x[tx[0]], y[tx[0]], r[tr[0]], ry[tr[0]])\n\n    def cost(z1, z2):\n        d = torch.cdist(z1[:, :, :-1], z2[:, :, :-1]).square() / 2\n        return d + torch.as_tensor(W)[z1[:, :, -1].long().unsqueeze(2),\n                                      z2[:, :, -1].long().unsqueeze(1)] / 2\n\n    potential = SamplesLoss('sinkhorn', p=2, blur=np.sqrt(.1), debias=False,\n                            potentials=True, cost=cost, backend='tensorized')\n\n    reg = 0.1\n    F = {}\n    batchcost = np.zeros((len(tx), len(tr)))\n\n    for i, idx in enumerate(tx):\n        for j, jdx in enumerate(tr):\n            a = x[idx]; b = r[jdx]\n            z1 = torch.tensor(np.column_stack([a, y[idx]]), dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            z2 = torch.tensor(np.column_stack([b, ry[jdx] + 10]), dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            with torch.inference_mode():\n                f_t, g_t = potential(z1, z2)\n            f_np = f_t.numpy().ravel().astype(np.float64)\n            g_np = g_t.numpy().ravel().astype(np.float64)\n\n            n_src = len(idx); n_tgt = len(jdx)\n            a_w = 1.0 / n_src\n            b_w = 1.0 / n_tgt\n\n            # Reconstruct cost matrix to compute batchcost from potentials\n            C_eucl = cdist(a, b, 'sqeuclidean') / 2.0\n            C_label = W[y[idx[:, None]], ry[jdx[None, :]] + 10] / 2.0\n            C = C_eucl + C_label\n\n            # P_ij = a_i * b_j * exp((f_i + g_j - C_ij) / reg)\n            P = a_w * b_w * np.exp((f_np[:, None] + g_np[None, :] - C) / reg)\n            batchcost[i, j] = float(np.sum(P * C)) / (n_src + n_tgt)\n\n            F[i, j] = (f_np - f_np.mean()) * n_src / (n_src - 1)\n\n    Q = ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(tx)), ot.unif(len(tr)),\n                    batchcost / max(float(batchcost.max()), 1e-12), .01,\n                    numItermax=10000, stopThr=1e-10)\n    residual = max(np.max(np.abs(Q.sum(1) - ot.unif(len(tx)))),\n                   np.max(np.abs(Q.sum(0) - ot.unif(len(tr)))))\n    if residual > 1e-6:\n        raise ValueError(f'Unconverged batch transport: {residual}')\n\n    values = np.zeros(len(x))\n    for i, idx in enumerate(tx):\n        values[idx] = sum(Q[i, j] * F[i, j] for j in range(len(tr)))\n    return values\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
