{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_83", "type": "reasoning", "text": "Now I understand:\n\n- GeomLoss uses epsilon-scaling by default. \n\nI’ve clarified the working mechanism of GeomLoss' epsilon-scaling, including its convergence characteristic. It has been found that GeomLoss' v10 potentials are less accurate than POT's Sinkhorn, and the final value calculation only relies on GeomLoss' F (the Q term is only a batch weight), so GeomLoss' under-converged potentials can be used directly.\n\nIt has been confirmed that GeomLoss F works properly for the canonical method as both sides use the same F. The previous v10 error stemmed from incorrect batchcost calculation and wrong Q matrix, so I first need to correct both to exactly match the canonical output.\n\nI’ve confirmed there’s no need for exact matching since the quality gates are loose. The runtime bottleneck is the slow POT Sinkhorn for batchcost, so I’ll prioritize speeding it up with a cheaper Q approximation or converged GeomLoss-based batchcost calculation. Replacing it could cut total runtime by more than half, and I’ve found the GeomLoss batchcost estimation error comes from under-converged potentials and incorrect reconstruction.\n\nEven with perfect reconstruction, transport costs from GeomLoss and POT differ due to their distinct effective regularization. Both batch Q and F use Sinkhorn with different regularization strengths, and OT-based Q is a coarse approximation. The F matrices across reference batches have a 0.93 correlation, so uniform weighting works well enough. I’ll adopt the simplified solution of keeping GeomLoss for F and using uniform Q weighting, which will be a huge win if it passes the quality gates.\n\nI’ll test the simplified solution across multiple diverse cases instead of just one, as the evaluator has 30 varied test scenarios. I’ve realized the canonical Q is nearly uniform due to extremely strong regularization, so I’ll prioritize testing using the precomputed GeomLoss loss value as a batch cost proxy, which works well enough as long as its relative ordering is roughly accurate.\n"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_84", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/test_fast_q.py << 'PYEOF'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Test fast Q approximations: use GeomLoss S_eps as batchcost proxy.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport numpy as np, sys, time\nsys.path.insert(0, '/workspace/solution')\n\nimport torch\nfrom geomloss import SamplesLoss\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\nfrom scipy.stats import spearmanr\nimport ot\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(2)\n\ndef run_canonical(x, y, r, ry, seed=17, batch_size=1024):\n    x=np.asarray(x,np.float32); r=np.asarray(r,np.float32)\n    y=np.asarray(y,np.int64); ry=np.asarray(ry,np.int64)\n    tx=[np.arange(i,min(i+batch_size,len(x))) for i in range(0,len(x),batch_size)]\n    tr=[np.arange(i,min(i+batch_size,len(r))) for i in range(0,len(r),batch_size)]\n    xx=torch.tensor(np.concatenate([x[tx[0]],r[tr[0]]]),dtype=torch.float32)\n    yy=np.concatenate([y[tx[0]],ry[tr[0]]+10])\n    W=np.zeros((20,20),dtype=np.float32)\n    loss=SamplesLoss('sinkhorn',p=2,blur=np.sqrt(.1),debias=False,backend='tensorized')\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n        for i in range(20):\n            for j in range(i+1,20):\n                W[i,j]=W[j,i]=float(loss(xx[yy==i],xx[yy==j]))\n    def cost(z1,z2):\n        d=torch.cdist(z1[:,:,:-1],z2[:,:,:-1]).square()/2\n        return d+torch.as_tensor(W)[z1[:,:,-1].long().unsqueeze(2),z2[:,:,-1].long().unsqueeze(1)]/2\n    potential=SamplesLoss('sinkhorn',p=2,blur=np.sqrt(.1),debias=False,\n                         potentials=True,cost=cost,backend='tensorized')\n    loss_fn = SamplesLoss('sinkhorn', p=2, blur=np.sqrt(.1), debias=False, cost=cost, backend='tensorized')\n    F={}; batchcost=np.zeros((len(tx),len(tr)))\n    bc_sinkhorn = np.zeros((len(tx), len(tr)))\n    for i,idx in enumerate(tx):\n        for j,jdx in enumerate(tr):\n            a=x[idx];b=r[jdx]\n            # POT batchcost (slow, canonical)\n            C=cdist(a,b,'sqeuclidean')/2+W[y[idx,None],ry[jdx][None,:]+10]/2\n            P=ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(idx)),ot.unif(len(jdx)),C/max(float(C.max()),1e-12),.1)\n            batchcost[i,j]=float(np.sum(P*C))/(len(idx)+len(jdx))\n            \n            # GeomLoss F (fast, canonical)\n            z1=torch.tensor(np.column_stack([a,y[idx]]),dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            z2=torch.tensor(np.column_stack([b,ry[jdx]+10]),dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            with torch.inference_mode():\n                f_t,_=potential(z1,z2)\n                s_eps = float(loss_fn(z1, z2))\n            f=f_t.numpy().ravel().astype(float)\n            F[i,j]=(f-f.mean())*len(f)/(len(f)-1)\n            bc_sinkhorn[i, j] = s_eps\n    \n    Q_canon = ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(tx)), ot.unif(len(tr)),\n                          batchcost/max(float(batchcost.max()),1e-12),.01,\n                          numItermax=10000,stopThr=1e-10)\n    \n    Q_fast = ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(tx)), ot.unif(len(tr)),\n                         bc_sinkhorn/max(float(bc_sinkhorn.max()),1e-12),.01,\n                         numItermax=10000,stopThr=1e-10)\n    \n    def q_values(Q):\n        vals = np.zeros(len(x))\n        for i, idx in enumerate(tx):\n            vals[idx] = sum(Q[i,j] * F[i,j] for j in range(len(tr)))\n        return vals\n    \n    v_canon = q_values(Q_canon)\n    v_fast = q_values(Q_fast)\n    v_unif = q_values(np.ones((len(tx), len(tr))) / (len(tx) * len(tr)))\n    \n    return v_canon, v_fast, v_unif, batchcost, bc_sinkhorn, Q_canon, Q_fast\n\ndef nrmse(pred, target):\n    return np.sqrt(np.mean((pred - target)**2)) / np.std(target)\n\ndef top_q_overlap(a, b, q=0.25):\n    n = len(a)\n    k = int(n * q)\n    top_a = set(np.argsort(-a)[:k])\n    top_b = set(np.argsort(-b)[:k])\n    return len(top_a & top_b) / k\n\ncases = [\n    'seed_101_uniform_labels',\n    'seed_101_gaussian_016',\n    'seed_202_mixed',\n    'seed_404_gaussian_024',\n    'seed_505_asymmetric_labels',\n]\n\nfor case_id in cases:\n    d = np.load(f'/workspace/environment/public_assets/dev/{case_id}.npz')\n    x, y, r, ry, seed = d['x'], d['y'], d['r'], d['ry'], int(d['seed'])\n    \n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    v_c, v_f, v_u, bc_c, bc_s, Q_c, Q_s = run_canonical(x, y, r, ry, seed=seed)\n    t1 = time.perf_counter()\n    \n    print(f\\\"\\\\n=== {case_id} ({t1-t0:.2f}s) ===\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Batchcost canonical: {bc_c.ravel()}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Batchcost S_eps:     {bc_s.ravel()}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Batchcost rank corr: {spearmanr(bc_c.ravel(), bc_s.ravel())[0]:.4f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Q canonical: {Q_c.ravel()}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Q S_eps:     {Q_s.ravel()}\\\")\n    \n    print(f\\\"  NRMSE (S_eps Q):  {nrmse(v_f, v_c):.5f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Spearman (S_eps Q): {spearmanr(v_f, v_c)[0]:.5f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  TopQ (S_eps Q):   {top_q_overlap(v_f, v_c):.5f}\\\")\n    \n    print(f\\\"  NRMSE (uniform Q):  {nrmse(v_u, v_c):.5f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Spearman (uniform Q): {spearmanr(v_u, v_c)[0]:.5f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  TopQ (uniform Q):   {top_q_overlap(v_u, v_c):.5f}\\\")\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/test_fast_q.py 2>&1 | grep -v UserWarning | grep -v \\\"warnings.warn\\\"\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_84", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/test_fast_q.py << 'PYEOF'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Test fast Q approximations: use GeomLoss S_eps as batchcost proxy.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport numpy as np, sys, time\nsys.path.insert(0, '/workspace/solution')\n\nimport torch\nfrom geomloss import SamplesLoss\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\nfrom scipy.stats import spearmanr\nimport ot\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(2)\n\ndef run_canonical(x, y, r, ry, seed=17, batch_size=1024):\n    x=np.asarray(x,np.float32); r=np.asarray(r,np.float32)\n    y=np.asarray(y,np.int64); ry=np.asarray(ry,np.int64)\n    tx=[np.arange(i,min(i+batch_size,len(x))) for i in range(0,len(x),batch_size)]\n    tr=[np.arange(i,min(i+batch_size,len(r))) for i in range(0,len(r),batch_size)]\n    xx=torch.tensor(np.concatenate([x[tx[0]],r[tr[0]]]),dtype=torch.float32)\n    yy=np.concatenate([y[tx[0]],ry[tr[0]]+10])\n    W=np.zeros((20,20),dtype=np.float32)\n    loss=SamplesLoss('sinkhorn',p=2,blur=np.sqrt(.1),debias=False,backend='tensorized')\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n        for i in range(20):\n            for j in range(i+1,20):\n                W[i,j]=W[j,i]=float(loss(xx[yy==i],xx[yy==j]))\n    def cost(z1,z2):\n        d=torch.cdist(z1[:,:,:-1],z2[:,:,:-1]).square()/2\n        return d+torch.as_tensor(W)[z1[:,:,-1].long().unsqueeze(2),z2[:,:,-1].long().unsqueeze(1)]/2\n    potential=SamplesLoss('sinkhorn',p=2,blur=np.sqrt(.1),debias=False,\n                         potentials=True,cost=cost,backend='tensorized')\n    loss_fn = SamplesLoss('sinkhorn', p=2, blur=np.sqrt(.1), debias=False, cost=cost, backend='tensorized')\n    F={}; batchcost=np.zeros((len(tx),len(tr)))\n    bc_sinkhorn = np.zeros((len(tx), len(tr)))\n    for i,idx in enumerate(tx):\n        for j,jdx in enumerate(tr):\n            a=x[idx];b=r[jdx]\n            # POT batchcost (slow, canonical)\n            C=cdist(a,b,'sqeuclidean')/2+W[y[idx,None],ry[jdx][None,:]+10]/2\n            P=ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(idx)),ot.unif(len(jdx)),C/max(float(C.max()),1e-12),.1)\n            batchcost[i,j]=float(np.sum(P*C))/(len(idx)+len(jdx))\n            \n            # GeomLoss F (fast, canonical)\n            z1=torch.tensor(np.column_stack([a,y[idx]]),dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            z2=torch.tensor(np.column_stack([b,ry[jdx]+10]),dtype=torch.float32)[None]\n            with torch.inference_mode():\n                f_t,_=potential(z1,z2)\n                s_eps = float(loss_fn(z1, z2))\n            f=f_t.numpy().ravel().astype(float)\n            F[i,j]=(f-f.mean())*len(f)/(len(f)-1)\n            bc_sinkhorn[i, j] = s_eps\n    \n    Q_canon = ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(tx)), ot.unif(len(tr)),\n                          batchcost/max(float(batchcost.max()),1e-12),.01,\n                          numItermax=10000,stopThr=1e-10)\n    \n    Q_fast = ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(len(tx)), ot.unif(len(tr)),\n                         bc_sinkhorn/max(float(bc_sinkhorn.max()),1e-12),.01,\n                         numItermax=10000,stopThr=1e-10)\n    \n    def q_values(Q):\n        vals = np.zeros(len(x))\n        for i, idx in enumerate(tx):\n            vals[idx] = sum(Q[i,j] * F[i,j] for j in range(len(tr)))\n        return vals\n    \n    v_canon = q_values(Q_canon)\n    v_fast = q_values(Q_fast)\n    v_unif = q_values(np.ones((len(tx), len(tr))) / (len(tx) * len(tr)))\n    \n    return v_canon, v_fast, v_unif, batchcost, bc_sinkhorn, Q_canon, Q_fast\n\ndef nrmse(pred, target):\n    return np.sqrt(np.mean((pred - target)**2)) / np.std(target)\n\ndef top_q_overlap(a, b, q=0.25):\n    n = len(a)\n    k = int(n * q)\n    top_a = set(np.argsort(-a)[:k])\n    top_b = set(np.argsort(-b)[:k])\n    return len(top_a & top_b) / k\n\ncases = [\n    'seed_101_uniform_labels',\n    'seed_101_gaussian_016',\n    'seed_202_mixed',\n    'seed_404_gaussian_024',\n    'seed_505_asymmetric_labels',\n]\n\nfor case_id in cases:\n    d = np.load(f'/workspace/environment/public_assets/dev/{case_id}.npz')\n    x, y, r, ry, seed = d['x'], d['y'], d['r'], d['ry'], int(d['seed'])\n    \n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    v_c, v_f, v_u, bc_c, bc_s, Q_c, Q_s = run_canonical(x, y, r, ry, seed=seed)\n    t1 = time.perf_counter()\n    \n    print(f\\\"\\\\n=== {case_id} ({t1-t0:.2f}s) ===\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Batchcost canonical: {bc_c.ravel()}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Batchcost S_eps:     {bc_s.ravel()}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Batchcost rank corr: {spearmanr(bc_c.ravel(), bc_s.ravel())[0]:.4f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Q canonical: {Q_c.ravel()}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Q S_eps:     {Q_s.ravel()}\\\")\n    \n    print(f\\\"  NRMSE (S_eps Q):  {nrmse(v_f, v_c):.5f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Spearman (S_eps Q): {spearmanr(v_f, v_c)[0]:.5f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  TopQ (S_eps Q):   {top_q_overlap(v_f, v_c):.5f}\\\")\n    \n    print(f\\\"  NRMSE (uniform Q):  {nrmse(v_u, v_c):.5f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  Spearman (uniform Q): {spearmanr(v_u, v_c)[0]:.5f}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"  TopQ (uniform Q):   {top_q_overlap(v_u, v_c):.5f}\\\")\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/test_fast_q.py 2>&1 | grep -v UserWarning | grep -v \\\"warnings.warn\\\"\"", "aggregated_output": "\n=== seed_101_uniform_labels (3.77s) ===\n  Batchcost canonical: [1.07772802 1.08187078 1.05018671 1.05517999 1.08467474 1.14912821]\n  Batchcost S_eps:     [418.79159546 419.40042114 419.48999023 430.67037964 436.03405762\n 444.32730103]\n  Batchcost rank corr: 0.5429\n  Q canonical: [0.08355218 0.24978115 0.08827109 0.24506225 0.32817673 0.0051566 ]\n  Q S_eps:     [0.06537723 0.2679561  0.24161211 0.09172122 0.19301065 0.14032268]\n  NRMSE (S_eps Q):  0.13436\n  Spearman (S_eps Q): 0.97574\n  TopQ (S_eps Q):   0.96533\n  NRMSE (uniform Q):  0.12910\n  Spearman (uniform Q): 0.97844\n  TopQ (uniform Q):   0.96400\n\n=== seed_101_gaussian_016 (2.21s) ===\n  Batchcost canonical: [0.95715189 0.963699   0.93247565 0.93861755 0.95474424 0.96708356]\n  Batchcost S_eps:     [226.62911987 226.31510925 228.88139343