{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_86", "type": "reasoning", "text": "Interesting findings:\n\n1. \n\nPoor batch cost correlations and unqualified S_eps Q approaches have been found, with uniform Q performing slightly better but still unable to guarantee full quality gate passes. The Q matrix significantly impacts results, so a more accurate batch cost calculation method is needed. GeomLoss potentials are underconverged with mismatched effective regularization from POT, and canonical normalization slows Sinkhorn convergence, so three optimization approaches will be tested.\n\nThe first optimization approach will be implementing a fast log-domain Sinkhorn with ~100 iterations and adjusted convergence thresholds. I'll first profile time consumption to verify if fewer iterations can effectively boost efficiency.\n"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_87", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/test_sinkhorn_speed.py << 'PYEOF'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Profile POT sinkhorn time breakdown and test faster variants.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\nimport ot\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\n\ntorch.set_num_threads = lambda x: None\n\n# Simulate a realistic case\nnp.random.seed(42)\nn, m = 1024, 1024\na_np = np.random.randn(n, 10).astype(np.float32) * 2\nb_np = np.random.randn(m, 10).astype(np.float32) * 2\n\n# Cost matrix\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nC = cdist(a_np, b_np, 'sqeuclidean') / 2.0\nt1 = time.perf_counter()\nprint(f\\\"Cost matrix (1024x1024): {t1-t0:.3f}s, C_max={C.max():.1f}\\\")\n\n# Canonical POT sinkhorn\nalpha = ot.unif(n)\nbeta = ot.unif(m)\nC_norm = C / C.max()\nreg = 0.1\n\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nP = ot.sinkhorn(alpha, beta, C_norm, reg, numItermax=10000)\nt1 = time.perf_counter()\nprint(f\\\"POT sinkhorn (numItermax=10000): {t1-t0:.3f}s\\\")\nprint(f\\\"  residual: {abs(P.sum(1)-alpha).max():.2e}\\\")\ncost = np.sum(P * C_norm)\nprint(f\\\"  normalized transport cost: {cost:.6f}\\\")\n\n# Fewer iterations\nfor iters in [500, 200, 100, 50]:\n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    P2 = ot.sinkhorn(alpha, beta, C_norm, reg, numItermax=iters)\n    t1 = time.perf_counter()\n    cost2 = np.sum(P2 * C_norm)\n    print(f\\\"POT sinkhorn (numItermax={iters}): {t1-t0:.3f}s, \\\"\n          f\\\"residual={abs(P2.sum(1)-alpha).max():.2e}, \\\"\n          f\\\"cost_err={abs(cost2-cost)/cost:.6f}\\\")\n\n# Log-domain sinkhorn\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nP_log = ot.bregman.sinkhorn_log(alpha, beta, C_norm, reg, numItermax=10000)\nt1 = time.perf_counter()\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nPOT sinkhorn_log (numItermax=10000): {t1-t0:.3f}s\\\")\ncost_log = np.sum(P_log * C_norm)\nprint(f\\\"  cost: {cost_log:.6f} (diff from standard: {abs(cost_log-cost)/cost:.6f})\\\")\n\nfor iters in [500, 200, 100, 50]:\n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    P_log2 = ot.bregman.sinkhorn_log(alpha, beta, C_norm, reg, numItermax=iters)\n    t1 = time.perf_counter()\n    cost2 = np.sum(P_log2 * C_norm)\n    print(f\\\"POT sinkhorn_log (numItermax={iters}): {t1-t0:.3f}s, \\\"\n          f\\\"residual={abs(P_log2.sum(1)-alpha).max():.2e}, \\\"\n          f\\\"cost_err={abs(cost2-cost)/cost:.6f}\\\")\n\n# Stabilized sinkhorn\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nP_stab = ot.bregman.sinkhorn_stabilized(alpha, beta, C_norm, reg, numItermax=10000)\nt1 = time.perf_counter()\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nPOT sinkhorn_stabilized (numItermax=10000): {t1-t0:.3f}s\\\")\ncost_stab = np.sum(P_stab * C_norm)\nprint(f\\\"  cost: {cost_stab:.6f}\\\")\n\n# Let's also test with the actual effective reg from canonical\n# C_max ~ 20000, reg=0.1 means effective reg = 0.1 * C_max = 2000\n# That's very strong regularization. The Sinkhorn should converge very fast.\n# Wait, no: POT uses reg=0.1 with C normalized to max 1.\n# Effective reg / C_max = 0.1, which is quite strong.\n\n# How many iterations does POT actually run?\nP3, log = ot.sinkhorn(alpha, beta, C_norm, reg, numItermax=10000, log=True)\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nPOT actually ran {log['niter']} iterations\\\")\nprint(f\\\"  final error: {log['log_err'][-1]:.2e}\\\")\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/test_sinkhorn_speed.py\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
